On Oct 25, 2011, at 8:11 AM, James W. MacDonald wrote:

> Hi Michael,
>
> On 10/24/2011 3:21 PM, Michael Muratet wrote:
>> Greetings
>>
>> This has probably been answered before, but I can't narrow the  
>> search down enough to find it in the archives. I am looking at the  
>> output from and documentation for eBayes and realized that the null  
>> hypothesis for the F statistic is that all the expression values  
>> are zero. I want to test the hypothesis that all the expression  
>> values are equal, i.e., rejection implies differential expression.  
>> I see from the topTable documentation that calling it with  
>> coef=NULL will yield an F statistic calculation, and I infer from  
>> the docs it will include all the conditions. What is the null  
>> hypothesis: that all the values are equal, or that all the values  
>> are zero?
>
> I think you misunderstood the help for eBayes(). It states that the  
> F-statistic tests that all _contrasts_ are zero, which is not the  
> same as all expression values equal to zero (which wouldn't make  
> sense).
>
> If a contrast is equal to zero, it implies no differential  
> expression between the samples compared in that contrast (or more  
> correctly, a sufficiently small F-statistic implies that you are  
> unable to reject the null hypothesis of a difference in any  
> contrast). Note that you are only testing those contrasts that you  
> specified via a contrasts matrix, or specified indirectly via your  
> design matrix.
>
> Best,
>
> Jim
